<title>USA: Shell Capline July crude nominations 1,131,026 bpd.</title>
<headline>Shell Capline July crude nominations 1,131,026 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil Co said on Tuesday that nominations on the Capline crude oil pipeline for July totalled 1,131,026 barrels per day (bpd).</p>
<p>The actual allocation on the pipeline for June was 1,122,549 bpd, compared with nominations for that month of 1,125,433 bpd.</p>
<p>The pipeline, a major artery linking the Gulf Coast and the Midwest, has a capacity to run 1.11 million bpd and is operated by Shell.</p>
<p>The 40-inch line runs from the St. James terminal in Louisiana north to the Patoka terminal in Illinois.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
